.github/actions/run/action.yml:11:41: untrusted input "inputs.ref" is written to $GITHUB_ENV. an attacker who controls the value can set LD_PRELOAD or NODE_OPTIONS (a newline adds another variable) and run code in the next steps. do not write input that an outsider controls to $GITHUB_ENV; validate it first or pass it to the next step with $GITHUB_OUTPUT [github-env]
.github/actions/run/action.yml:15:14: this step checks out code from a pull request (github.event.pull_request.head.sha) in a "pull_request_target" workflow and "make" runs it afterwards. the workflow has a write token and secrets, so whoever controls that code can use them. run untrusted code in a "pull_request" workflow without secrets, or check out the base branch and only read the pull request as data [untrusted-checkout]
